      {
        "id": 29277,
        "name": "beevolant",
        "username": "beevolant",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/8edcca/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-14T16:41:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>They only printed a limited number of the promo cards, so I’m betting with Husemann that there wont be any more Young Legacy or Promo Wraith cards being added to the market after the end of the IR kickstarter. If you don’t get them through the Kickstarter, you’re probably SOL.</p>\n<p>My guess is that if the OP’s friend is at GenCon or PAX Prime this year, s/he will be able to score at least one of the two IR promo cards with IR purchase (Fanatic or Ra) and probably one of the two Expanded Ed promo cards with purchase (Blade or Omnitron). I doubt they’d give two promo cards free per game - but maybe? That would be very generous of them, especially when we know that they will probably do future kickstarters for expansions and would want those promo cards to be made available to future backers.</p>\n<p>I’m guessing that Unity and Ambuscade decks will probably be available for purchase on the SotM website and at their booths at conventions - I’m doubting that those decks will be sold to distrubutors for gaming stores, but who knows, they might be.</p>",
        "post_number": 9,
        "post_type": 1,
